enonce_intro_markdown:
An inter-urban transport company carries out the following activities amongst others:

- cash office collects transport fares from clients;
- clients pay fare online using electronic money transfer;
- clients make travel reservations;
- workers are paid every two weeks;
- correspondences are sent to partners of the transport company;
- buses and their respective drivers are scheduled on weekly basis.

questions.corrige_markdown:
**Use of graphics software (2 marks)**

Graphics software is used to create and edit pictures and designs. The company can use it to:

- design attractive posters, flyers, banners, adverts and the logo of the company, and the painting on the buses, so that more clients are attracted;
- design tickets, route maps, timetables and price lists that are easy for clients to read;
- present information such as the number of passengers per month as charts and graphs for the management.
